After returning from the mines I found an archaic floor and below that I
received a psionic message from the local Organization.  I know better than
to ignore one of those, so I found his portal and went to see the man.  He
had his own muscle, big and dumb. But was looking for a smart guy to get
some special Key from a guy who does Work.  Wonderful I gotta do this thing
for Kos and now the local boss want me to shine an assassin.  I always do my
homework, so I dig out a ring I found earlier that allows one to control
shapechanges and headed down.  After fighting my way down I found that there
were no more stairs down and the Assassin was nowhere to be seen.  Stripping
off my armor I used my spell of change on myself (it took a few tries, I
wasn't that powerful, especially without my robe of power) becoming a
mythical beast with the ability to phase through rock.  I remembered that
these beasts could eat magical totems and had a chance to keep the property.
I managed to become resistant to electricity this way but lost my ability to
survive without air.  Verra seldom smiles all the time.  I phased through
the wall and spotted the assassin.  He picked up the key and teleported over
to me.  I realized that he could teleport here and I couldn't.  I backed
away through the wall and he followed me.  It took me a while to kill him
but the Magicbane finally did him in.  I got the key and a silver bell that
looked special.  It must have been, I couldn't stick it in the bag.
Returning to the local boss, he told me I should hold onto the Key and show
it to the Kos guy when I see him.  Some thanks.



A level below the portal I found another temple to Kos.  I didn't have a lot
of gold so he didn't get rich.  A floor or two later I found another unlucky
adventurer, this time she was undead and trying to suck my blood out along
with another Vampire.  She and her companion were offed and her grave
yielded a hammer named mo-something that I stashed and a lamp that was still
burning.  Who knows how long that vampire was here, but that lamp must be
special to still be burning.  I used some of Kos' water to bless it and held
onto it for light.



I was getting a bit tired, it had been twenty five floors of this, not
counting the mines, the boulder puzzle, and the boss thief's area.  But an
island surrounded by water was a sign that I was close.  I'd heard about the
Gorgon, Medusa.  I had a towel to wrap around my head, and a wand that shot
cold to freeze the lake for the crossing.  One annoyance that I found here
were these little gremlin things that kept jumping into the water and
multiplying.  They weren't hostile, so I just moved around them.  Medusa
apparently couldn't stand the sight of her reflection in my dragonscale
armor.  Down again, to a large castle.  The fight here was just as hard as
the fight in the fort in it's own way.  In the audience chamber I decided to
try the view from the throne.  A voice asked me what species I wanted to
destroy.  I thought about dealing with those tentacled things, but decided
to live and let live.  "None"  I found a side room with a chest standing on
a special word.  I opened the chest and found a wand.  Testing it allowed me
to have a wish fulfilled.



