I have to shine a wizard this time.  I knew this would have to be done, I'd
been told that this wizard had the book that would allow me to perform the
ritual to open the way to my last target and the item that Kos needed.  The
wizard's tower was a tough slog, but I reached his antechamber.  A Spell of
Dig opened his inner chamber and he jumped at me.  My boss Vlad has a
saying. A dagger between the shoulder-blades will cramp the style of even
the greatest wizard.  I found a new one.  A wand of death will kill even the
most annoying wizard.  Book in hand I headed back down.  Shortly before
leaving his tower I hear "So you thought you could kill me, fool?"
Apparently this guy won't stay dead.  I hit him with the wand again.  Down
to the square, retrieving the bell and candlestick, it's ritual time.  I
realize that I have no candles.  I fish out the wand from the castle and
wish for seven candles.  Ok, lights, bell, read.  The way to the sanctum is
opened.  The last target is a priest.  The temple is well guarded and I
fight my way through.   I decide that whatever god this temple is dedicated
to might take it personally if I kill the priest inside, so I step in, he
gets pissed steps toward me, I back out and start throwing daggers.  Six
daggers later the priest is dead and I have the bauble Kos was looking for.
I pull out a potion from my bag and rise through the temple's roof.  (many
want to make a stylish entrance, I prefer a timely exit.)  On the way back I
encounter a strange force that wants me to stay.  It really wants me to stay
on the 47th floor, I have to traverse it no less than six times.  I also
make a pit stop at Vlad the Impaled's tower and pray to Kos.  He halls me
the "hand of Arioch" and tells me to steal souls in his name.  The
broadsword Stormbringer joins the other named weapons in the Bag.  The
Wizard made another appearance along the way, and actually made another of
